    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0eb83e14_70b6cac5",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/mem_protect.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2139,
      "author": {
        "id": 1569742
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-11T08:11:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reasoning was that the MODULE_OWNED state can be \u0027additive\u0027 to other states (e.g. RESTRICTED_PROT), though in practice these other additive states are not stored in the struct hyp_page I think, so this was mostly forward looking (we could decide to cache the RESTRICTED_PROT state in hyp_page as well to avoid inferring from the PTE).\n\nI\u0027ll double check that setting this to \u0027\u003d\u0027 here doesn\u0027t break anything, but if so I\u0027ll update the patch, cheers.",
      "parentUuid": "1a2aca5e_ba286c75",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2139,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 2139,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "8950c6f0823f541298898209abf7eb02b2c44f82",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2501f473_bfe6b5fe",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/mem_protect.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2139,
      "author": {
        "id": 1569742
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-11T08:19:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, so MODULE_OWNED is additive to NOPAGE when a page is marked as owned by PKVM_ID_PROTECTED, so using \u0027\u003d\u0027 here would break that. I can\u0027t find anywhere where that would be a problem, so maybe it\u0027s OK, but this asymmetry is in fact consistent with the asymmetric state check further up in this function. Wdyt?",
      "parentUuid": "0eb83e14_70b6cac5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2139,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 2139,
        "endChar": 24
